.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt OSSL_CRMF_MSG_SET0_VALIDITY 3ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm OSSL_CRMF_MSG_set0_validity ,
.Nm OSSL_CRMF_MSG_set_certReqId ,
.Nm OSSL_CRMF_CERTTEMPLATE_fill ,
.Nm OSSL_CRMF_MSG_set0_extensions ,
.Nm OSSL_CRMF_MSG_push0_extension ,
.Nm OSSL_CRMF_MSG_create_popo ,
.Nm OSSL_CRMF_MSGS_verify_popo
.Nd functions populating and verifying CRMF CertReqMsg structures
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In openssl/crmf.h
.Ft int
.Fo OSSL_CRMF_MSG_set0_validity
.Fa "OSSL_CRMF_MSG *crm"
.Fa "ASN1_TIME *notBefore"
.Fa "ASN1_TIME *notAfter"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo OSSL_CRMF_MSG_set_certReqId
.Fa "OSSL_CRMF_MSG *crm"
.Fa "int rid"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo OSSL_CRMF_CERTTEMPLATE_fill
.Fa "OSSL_CRMF_CERTTEMPLATE *tmpl"
.Fa "EVP_PKEY *pubkey"
.Fa "const X509_NAME *subject"
.Fa "const X509_NAME *issuer"
.Fa "const ASN1_INTEGER *serial"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo OSSL_CRMF_MSG_set0_extensions
.Fa "OSSL_CRMF_MSG *crm"
.Fa "X509_EXTENSIONS *exts"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo OSSL_CRMF_MSG_push0_extension
.Fa "OSSL_CRMF_MSG *crm"
.Fa "X509_EXTENSION *ext"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo OSSL_CRMF_MSG_create_popo
.Fa "int meth"
.Fa "OSSL_CRMF_MSG *crm"
.Fa "EVP_PKEY *pkey"
.Fa "const EVP_MD *digest"
.Fa "OSSL_LIB_CTX *libctx"
.Fa "const char *propq"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo OSSL_CRMF_MSGS_verify_popo
.Fa "const OSSL_CRMF_MSGS *reqs"
.Fa "int rid"
.Fa "int acceptRAVerified"
.Fa "OSSL_LIB_CTX *libctx"
.Fa "const char *propq"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn OSSL_CRMF_MSG_set0_validity
sets the
.Fa notBefore
and
.Fa notAfter
fields as validity constraints in the certTemplate of
.Fa crm .
Any of the
.Fa notBefore
and
.Fa notAfter
parameters may be NULL, which means no constraint for the respective
field.
On success ownership of
.Fa notBefore
and
.Fa notAfter
is transferred to
.Fa crm .
.Pp
.Fn OSSL_CRMF_MSG_set_certReqId
sets
.Fa rid
as the certReqId of
.Fa crm .
.Pp
.Fn OSSL_CRMF_CERTTEMPLATE_fill
sets those fields of the certTemplate
.Fa tmpl
for which non-NULL values are provided:
.Fa pubkey ,
.Fa subject ,
.Fa issuer ,
and/or
.Fa serial .
X.509 extensions may be set using
.Fn OSSL_CRMF_MSG_set0_extensions .
On success the reference counter of the
.Fa pubkey
(if given) is incremented, while the
.Fa subject ,
.Fa issuer ,
and
.Fa serial
structures (if given) are copied.
.Pp
.Fn OSSL_CRMF_MSG_set0_extensions
sets
.Fa exts
as the extensions in the certTemplate of
.Fa crm .
Frees any pre-existing ones and consumes
.Fa exts .
.Pp
.Fn OSSL_CRMF_MSG_push0_extension
pushes the X509 extension
.Fa ext
to the extensions in the certTemplate of
.Fa crm .
Consumes
.Fa ext .
.Pp
.Fn OSSL_CRMF_MSG_create_popo
creates and sets the Proof-of-Possession (POPO) according to the method
.Fa meth
in
.Fa crm .
The library context
.Fa libctx
and property query string
.Fa propq ,
may be NULL to select the defaults.
In case the method is OSSL_CRMF_POPO_SIGNATURE the POPO is calculated
using the private key
.Fa pkey
and the digest method
.Fa digest ,
where the
.Fa digest
argument is ignored if
.Fa pkey
is of a type (such as Ed25519 and Ed448) that is implicitly associated
with a digest algorithm.
.Pp
.Fa meth
can be one of the following:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It * OSSL_CRMF_POPO_NONE - RFC 4211, section 4, POP field omitted. CA/RA uses out-of-band method to verify POP. Note that servers may fail in this case, resulting for instance in HTTP error code 500 (Internal error).
.It * OSSL_CRMF_POPO_RAVERIFIED - RFC 4211, section 4, explicit indication that the RA has already verified the POP.
.It * OSSL_CRMF_POPO_SIGNATURE - RFC 4211, section 4.1, only case 3 supported so far.
.It * OSSL_CRMF_POPO_KEYENC - RFC 4211, section 4.2, only indirect method (subsequentMessage/enccert) supported, challenge-response exchange (challengeResp) not yet supported.
.It * OSSL_CRMF_POPO_KEYAGREE - RFC 4211, section 4.3, not yet supported.
.El
OSSL_CRMF_MSGS_verify_popo verifies the Proof-of-Possession of the
request with the given
.Fa rid
in the list of
.Fa reqs .
Optionally accepts RAVerified.
It can make use of the library context
.Fa libctx
and property query string
.Fa propq .
.Sh RETURN VALUES
All functions return 1 on success, 0 on error.
.Sh SEE ALSO
RFC 4211
.Sh HISTORY
The OpenSSL CRMF support was added in OpenSSL 3.0.
